  <p>
    Money matters here as much as the syllabus. Treat about 10% of the total education budget as a starting cap
    for any single paid programme, and keep the rest for boards, tools, travel and the next skill. Going above
    roughly 20% needs course-specific evidence, such as verified placement numbers and real tool access. Do not
    take a loan for a short course.
  </p>

